>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `REFUTE_TAC`

``` hol4
Refute.REFUTE_TAC : Abbrev.tactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Searches for a counterexample to the current tactic goal.

`REFUTE_TAC` calls `Refute.refute_goal !Refute.the_config` on the supplied
goal, using every backend selected by the current configuration.  It prints
the resulting `Counterexample`, `NoCounterexample`, or `Unknown` report and
then applies `ALL_TAC`, leaving the goal unchanged in every case.  Thus this
is a diagnostic tactic, not a proof tactic: it never closes the goal and a
counterexample is not represented as tactic failure.

The tactic reads `the_config` when it is applied and honours every field,
including `quiet` and `expect`.

### Failure

A mismatch with a configured non-default expectation raises a HOL error.
Interrupts are re-raised.  Ordinary Refute outcomes do not make the tactic
fail.

